								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=254.msg16478#msg16478"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=254.msg16478#msg16478">Re: Loyalist Shield of Honor</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #10 on:</b> April 15, 2005, 01:06:47 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							There have long been rumors that killing the named in the vamp castle can make that last rare spawn pop.&nbsp; I don&#039;t know if the rumors are true or not, but I did it back when I finished the shield quest.&nbsp; I had my warrior and cleric and needed something to do while I camped it anyway.&nbsp; After about 2 hours the mob I needed popped and I called in some guildies to finish off the quest.<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
<a name="lastPost"></a>
